{:edb/db-before-t 1010 :edb/db-after-t 1011 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534323 50 #inst "2026-10-11T19:10:48.229Z" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186183194 13194139534323 17592186045417 false] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186183195 13194139534323 17592186045417 false] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186183196 13194139534323 17592186045417 false] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186183197 13194139534323 17592186045417 false] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186183198 13194139534323 17592186045417 false] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418998 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419001 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419002 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419003 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186183193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419004 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186183193 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418998 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186184196 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419007 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186184764 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186184764 1071 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[A1] - [A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *If $w$ is a vector such that $x + w = x$ for some $x ∈ V$, then $w = 0$.*\n\n*Proof:*\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x + w|= x & [given] \\\\ (x + w) + (-x)|= x + (-x) & [add- xto both sides] \\\\ (w + x) + (-x)|= x + (-x) & [axiom __] \\\\ w + (x + (-x))|= x + (-x) & [axiom A2] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 false] [17592186184764 1071 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $w=0.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186184764 1074 "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A1}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419008 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419009 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419010 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1045 "Defining Abstract Vector Spaces" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1046 #edb/ref 17592186419008 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049064 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418995 1053 #uuid "71036dcd-e882-527a-9681-dd5cc25371dc" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418996 1080 "multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418996 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418996 1083 #uuid "313cdc82-5d69-5af4-95bb-ace914a012ac" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418997 1080 "addition of functions in $A$  is not associative" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418997 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418997 1083 #uuid "4f43eb35-6698-556b-937a-7540b2eaa194" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418998 1080 "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418998 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418998 1083 #uuid "54174a8e-4b9f-5398-9c3e-042309cf5af7" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418999 1080 "addition of functions in $A$  is not commutative" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418999 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186418999 1083 #uuid "54d7d70f-b06b-5dba-8920-ce4be2335648" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419000 1080 "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in A$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419000 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419000 1083 #uuid "61ff392f-4de3-5c34-9123-789573d772b5" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419001 1080 "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419001 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419001 1083 #uuid "7c55b42e-8e25-5d4a-9c6c-fb23853f6637" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419002 1080 "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A4}$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419002 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419002 1083 #uuid "923e4cd4-7cb7-513f-a013-6b459182a21c" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419003 1080 "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A4}$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419003 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419003 1083 #uuid "c5a112ad-76a7-5358-b6fe-7be7dc9072ca" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419004 1080 "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419004 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419004 1083 #uuid "edaa960c-9666-5ef7-ae8f-8608f1b827e8" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419005 1080 "addition and scalar multiplication of functions  in $A$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419005 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419005 1083 #uuid "f187a6fa-78fb-565f-9a52-c1915abb65f1" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418996 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418997 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418999 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419000 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419005 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1077 "selection" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418996 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419006 1079 #uuid "4628fceb-08d9-5ba5-86ad-00d444e18706" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419007 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419006 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419007 1069 "q-94792" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419007 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419007 1071 "Let $A$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form  $f(x)=a+{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419007 1072 #uuid "1a47334c-0a05-5b9c-b7eb-76cf4c1d5cfb" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419007 1074 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because **multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)={x}^{2},$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2{x}^{2}.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin A$ because the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in A.$ $\\,✓$" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419008 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419010 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419008 1062 #uuid "2f729f32-9ccf-5071-9aab-348325a597e5" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419008 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184764 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419009 1062 #uuid "4418ef90-81d3-58b0-a3d7-e0c226069037" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419009 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419007 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419010 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419009 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419010 1062 #uuid "8de51b15-aacb-5258-b556-fea43597fd8c" 13194139534323 17592186045417 true] [17592186419010 1063 #edb/ref 17592186385324 13194139534323 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-71036dcd-e882-527a-9681-dd5cc25371dc" 17592186418995 "answer-313cdc82-5